. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         * I refrain from using the alternative specification using a 2SLS IV-
> regression, as I have serious concerns about the exclusion restriction being 
> violated. Thus, I stick with the main specification: linear OLS regression
. 
.         * Having Daughters (Daughters) leads to stronger support for Gender E
> quality (SuopportGE).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with SuopportG
> E as dependent variable and the dummy variable Daughters as independent varia
> ble, additionally controlling for total number of children (sumkids), income 
> (hghinc), education (pgbilzeit), marital status (partner), migration backgrou
> nd (migback), male (male) using heteroskedasticity robus standard errors
. 
.         regress SupportGE Daughters sumkids hghinc pgbilzeit ib1.partner ib1.
> migback i.male, robust

